---
description: DocForge CDOM schema and provider/export contract rules
alwaysApply: true
---

docforge-cdom:

- CDOM root fields: `schema_version`, `document_id`, `source`, `metadata`, `processing`, `pages`.
- Page fields include: `page_number`, `width`, `height`, `rotation`, `language`, `blocks`.
- Block fields include: `id`, `type`, `bbox`, `reading_order`, `confidence`, `language`, `text`, `children`, `attributes`.
- BBox format is always `[x1, y1, x2, y2]`.
- Initial block types: heading, paragraph, list, list_item, table, table_row, table_cell, image, code, formula, quote, page_break, unknown.
- Tables must preserve row/cell structure.
- Image blocks reference assets via `attributes.asset_id` (and optional `alt`).
- Block confidence is the minimum required confidence level.
- Layout providers own final `reading_order`.
- Processing metadata must record provider_name, provider_version, model_name, model_version, cdm_schema_version.
- Any schema evolution must stay backward-compatible for MVP unless explicitly approved.
- Provider SDK surfaces: OCRProvider, LayoutProvider, Exporter, PostProcessor.
- Provider selection may consider document type, language, capabilities, arch, CPU/GPU, health, priority — but selection stays outside providers themselves.
